  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I have a gun attached to one of my avatars that uses a sound emitter for a gunshot sound. I have it set to 0.1 volume and a maximum distance of 10m. It sounds rather quiet on my end. However, everyone else complains about it being extremely loud and they can hear it from clear across the level at exactly the same volume. In fact, I can hear the shot louder from the feedback of everyone else's microphones than I can directly from the emitter. I don't know why this is happening, maybe its a bug or maybe there is some setting in unity I don't know about.",
